  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 4.6,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings jump to about 0.93–0.95 at 6 h and stay flat with only noise, which looks like the reader hitting its ceiling. Diluted readings of the retained aliquots confirm this. The 18 h aliquot read 0.481 and 0.475 at 10× (back-calculated to about 4.78) and 0.114 and 0.111 at 40× (about 4.50). The two dilutions agree within about 6%, so the reader responds close to proportionally at these lower values, against an undiluted reading of 0.918. The 12 h aliquot read 0.227 at 20× (about 4.55), against an undiluted 0.910. The 6 h aliquot read 0.124 at 10× (about 1.24), against an undiluted 0.928, so the reading was already compressed by 6 h. The culture kept growing after 6 h and reached about 4.5–4.8 by 12–18 h. The undiluted readings understate late biomass about 5-fold. Best estimate at 18 h is about 4.6, the mean of the two dilution estimates."
  },
